            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0526" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.51/1728: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Eberhardt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-02-11T11:00:00-05:45"><hi rendition="#italic">February 11,
                                1927—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 1:25
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>41. Legation’s 38, February 9, 9 p.m. Keilhauer is now deposed [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">disposed?</hi>] to grant request of Nicaragua for loan
                    of $600,000 at 8 percent with security as already stated and an option of one
                    year on purchase of 51 percent or more or [<hi rendition="#italic">of</hi>]
                    stock in the national railroad of Nicaragua for American company. Cable urgently
                    if this agreeable to Department.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Eberhardt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
